Third-party parts that come with it:
- Lua 5.4 (MIT license, PUC-Rio), built into the program through the mlua crate
  (MIT license).
- The Rust crates listed in Cargo.lock, each under its own license (MIT or
  Apache-2.0 for nearly all, all permissive at the time of writing).
- DejaVu Sans Mono (Bitstream Vera license; DejaVu changes are in the public domain):
  its glyphs, as a bitmap, are the text of the window (src/native/font.bin). The license
  is in src/native/FONT-LICENSE.txt.
- Vosk (Apache License 2.0, Alpha Cephei Inc.), https://alphacephei.com/vosk: the
  speech recognizer. Not in the source; the Windows zip carries libvosk.dll with the
  runtime dlls of its compiler (libstdc++-6.dll and libgcc_s_seh-1.dll: GPL 3 with the GCC
  Runtime Library Exception; libwinpthread-1.dll: MIT and BSD style), as vosk publishes
  them. The russian model in lust-voice-ru.zip is vosk-model-small-ru-0.22 (Apache 2.0).
- tools/voice-check.wav: two words spoken by espeak-ng, made for the check of the voice.
